<title>SOUTH KOREA: Nichimen sells 6,000 tonnes Aussie wheat to Seoul.</title>
<headline>Nichimen sells 6,000 tonnes Aussie wheat to Seoul.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese trading house Nichimen Corp sold 6,000 tonnes of Australian wheat to a South Korean flour milling company, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said the deal was struck in a private negotiations between the two companies.</p>
<p>Nichimen sold 1,000 tonnes of Australian soft wheat, 4,000 tonnes of Australian soft white wheat and 1,000 tonnes of Australian hard wheat to the South Korean company, they said.</p>
<p>The identity of the South Korean company was not available.</p>
<p>Shipment was slated for January 20-February 20 to the South Korean port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
